      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: MR. KIRK O. KOLBO, ESQ., Minneapolis, Minnesota; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Kirk O. Kolbo",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Barbara Grutter applied for admission to the University of Michigan Law School with a personal right guaranteed by the Constitution that she would not have her race counted against her."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, of course, you -- I mean, a university or a law school is faced with a serious problem when it's one that gets thousands of applications for just a few slots. Where it has to be selective. And inherent in that setting is making choices about what students to admit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Olson",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Michigan law school admissions program fails every test this Court has articulated for evaluating governmental racial preferences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I think Santa Clara -- I think what Justice Scalia said bears modification, because in fact in Santa Clara, the highway dispatcher, there was a plus for sex, although there was no proven discrimination against that particular woman and this Court approved that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAHONEY: Your Honor it is not a quota."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "University of Michigan",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What the policy says, of course, is that it will only take race into account as long as it is necessary in order to achieve the educational objectives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Do we know what would be the increase of the named Plaintiffs, the increase in their chance of admission, were there no affirmative action programs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2002-02-241",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bec43eaf2ca32bef2b6a2c8929538a58f21fbe561d348debb2f26ab886326f61",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bec43eaf2ca3-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Constitution protects the rights of individuals, not racial groups."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
